---
import LegalLayout from '@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '@/data/site';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Credit Guide | Influx Financial"
  description="The Influx Financial Credit Guide, who we are, how we're paid, our lender panel, and how to raise concerns about our credit assistance."
  heading="Credit Guide"
  path="/credit-guide"
  lastUpdated={new Date('2026-07-01')}
>
  <p>
    <strong>
      [OWNER TO CONFIRM: A Credit Guide has prescribed content under the National Consumer Credit
      Protection Act. The AFCA membership number and the six most-used lenders below are still to be
      supplied by the licensee. Confirm this page against your licensee's approved Credit Guide
      template before launch.]
    </strong>
  </p>

  <h2>Who provides your credit assistance</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Business: {site.legalName}</li>
    <li>ABN: {site.regulatory.abn}</li>
    <li>
      Credit representative: {site.regulatory.creditRepName}, Australian Credit Representative {
        site.regulatory.creditRepNumber
      }
    </li>
    <li>
      Australian Credit Licence: {site.regulatory.acl} ({site.regulatory.aclHolder})
    </li>
    <li>Contact: {site.contact.phone} · {site.contact.email}</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Our lender panel</h2>
  <p>
    We access our panel of lenders through {site.regulatory.aggregator}, giving us a choice of more
    than 70 lenders. [OWNER TO CONFIRM: list of the six lenders with whom you conduct the most
    business, as required under the NCCP Act, to be supplied by the licensee.]
  </p>

  <h2>How we are paid</h2>
  <p>
    [OWNER TO CONFIRM: commission arrangements, upfront and trail commission ranges, any fees
    payable by the client, and how the client can request commission information.]
  </p>

  <h2>Best interests duty</h2>
  <p>
    When we provide credit assistance for regulated credit contracts, we are required to act in your
    best interests and to prioritise your interests over ours.
  </p>

  <h2>If something goes wrong</h2>
  <p>
    If you have a concern, please contact us first so we can try to put things right. You can reach
    us by phone on {site.contact.phone} or by email at {site.contact.email}, and we will acknowledge
    your concern and work with you to resolve it. If we cannot resolve your complaint, you may
    contact the Australian Financial Complaints Authority (AFCA), [OWNER TO CONFIRM: AFCA membership
    number], at afca.org.au or 1800 931 678.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
